You are an expert podcast script writer. Create an engaging, well-structured podcast script about the following topic for Medical professionals and policy makers. Duration: approximately 10 minutes.

Requirements:
1. Start with a compelling hook
2. Include a clear introduction
3. Organize body content into logical segments with transitions
4. Cite your sources when presenting facts
5. End with a strong conclusion and call to action
6. Use speaker labels and production cues where appropriate
7. Balance information density with entertainment

Verified facts to incorporate (cite these accurately):
[
  {
    "claim": "AI diagnostic tools achieve 94.5% accuracy in detecting diabetic retinopathy",
    "source": "Nature Medicine 2023"
  },
  {
    "claim": "The AI in healthcare market is projected to reach $187.95 billion by 2030",
    "source": "Statista"
  },
  {
    "claim": "FDA has approved over 500 AI/ML-enabled medical devices as of 2023",
    "source": "FDA AI/ML Device List"
  },
  {
    "claim": "AI can reduce drug discovery timelines from 10-15 years to 3-5 years",
    "source": "McKinsey 2023"
  },
  {
    "claim": "79% of healthcare organizations are currently using or planning to use AI",
    "source": "Deloitte 2024"
  },
  {
    "claim": "AI bias in training data can lead to 20-30% worse outcomes for underrepresented groups",
    "source": "JAMA 2023"
  },
  {
    "claim": "Medical errors are the third leading cause of death in the US, killing 250,000 annually",
    "source": "BMJ"
  },
  {
    "claim": "IBM Watson for Oncology made concordant treatment recommendations 93% of the time for certain cancers",
    "source": "Annals of Oncology"
  }
]

